1
00:00:04,130 --> 00:00:07,490
When Mr. Syngin went, it was beginning to snow.

2
00:00:08,389 --> 00:00:10,729
The whirling storm continued all night.

3
00:00:11,889 --> 00:00:15,789
The next day, a keen wind brought fresh and blinding falls.

4
00:00:16,529 --> 00:00:20,149
By twilight, the valley was drifted up and almost impassable.

5
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:26,050
I had closed my shutter, laid a mat to the door to prevent the snow from blowing in

6
00:00:26,051 --> 00:00:31,029
under it, trimmed my fire, and after sitting nearly an hour on the hearth

7
00:00:31,031 --> 00:00:34,983
listening to the muffled fury of the tempest, I

8
00:00:34,985 --> 00:00:38,710
lit a candle, took down Marmian and beginning.

9
00:00:40,149 --> 00:00:45,229
Day set on Norm's castled steep, and tweeds fair river broad and deep,

10
00:00:45,990 --> 00:00:50,910
and Chevyot's mountains loan, the massive towers, the dungeon keep, the flanking

11
00:00:50,910 --> 00:00:54,050
walls that round them sweep, in yellow lustre Sean.

12
00:00:55,149 --> 00:00:57,009
I soon forgot storm in music.

13
00:00:57,789 --> 00:00:58,789
I heard a noise.

14
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:01,029
The wind I thought shook the door.

15
00:01:01,410 --> 00:01:03,729
No, it was Syngin Rivers.

16
00:01:04,630 --> 00:01:05,630
Who?

17
00:01:05,710 --> 00:01:10,410
Lifting the latch came in out of the frozen hurricane, the howling darkness,

18
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:12,429
and stood before me.

19
00:01:13,229 --> 00:01:16,770
The cloak that covered his tall figure, all white as a glacier.

20
00:01:17,729 --> 00:01:21,135
I was almost in consternation, so little had I

21
00:01:21,137 --> 00:01:24,229
expected any guest from the blocked up veil that night.

22
00:01:25,809 --> 00:01:28,789
Any ill news, I demanded, has anything happened?

23
00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:33,050
No, how very easily alarmed you are.

24
00:01:33,929 --> 00:01:37,830
He answered, removing his cloak and hanging it up against the door,

25
00:01:38,529 --> 00:01:43,449
towards which he again coolly pushed the mat, which his entrance had deranged.

26
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,949
He stamped the snow from his boots.

27
00:01:46,910 --> 00:01:53,050
I shall sully the purity of your floor," said he, but you must excuse me for once.

28
00:01:54,009 --> 00:01:56,089
Then he approached the fire.

29
00:01:57,429 --> 00:02:00,853
I have had hard work to get here, I assure you, he

30
00:02:00,854 --> 00:02:03,330
observed, as he warmed his hands over the flame.

31
00:02:04,350 --> 00:02:08,949
One drift took me up to the waist, happily the snow is quite soft yet.

32
00:02:10,490 --> 00:02:12,330
But why are you come?

33
00:02:13,169 --> 00:02:14,649
I could not for bear saying.

34
00:02:15,610 --> 00:02:20,149
Rather an inhospitable question to put to a visitor, but since you ask it,

35
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:22,649
I answer simply to have a little talk with you.

36
00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:26,309
I got tired of my mute books and empty rooms.

37
00:02:27,830 --> 00:02:32,669
Besides, since yesterday I have experienced the excitement of a person to

38
00:02:32,671 --> 00:02:37,369
whom a tale has been half-tolled, and who is impatient to hear the sequel.

39
00:02:38,809 --> 00:02:40,009
He sat down.

40
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:44,638
I recalled his singular conduct of yesterday, and

41
00:02:44,638 --> 00:02:48,089
really, I began to fear his wits were touched.

42
00:02:48,830 --> 00:02:53,869
If he were insane, however, his was a very cool and collected insanity.

43
00:02:54,630 --> 00:02:59,589
I had never seen that handsome featured face of his look more like chiseled marble

44
00:02:59,591 --> 00:03:05,330
than it did just now, as he put aside his snow-wet hair from his forehead and let

45
00:03:05,331 --> 00:03:11,729
the fire light shine free on his pale brow and cheek as pale, where it grieved me to

46
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:16,690
discover the hollow trace of care or sorrow now so plainly graved.

47
00:03:17,350 --> 00:03:21,316
I waited, expecting he would say something I could at

48
00:03:21,317 --> 00:03:24,850
least comprehend, but his hand was now at his chin.

49
00:03:25,369 --> 00:03:29,047
His finger on his lip, he was thinking, it struck

50
00:03:29,048 --> 00:03:32,470
me, that his hand looked wasted like his face.

51
00:03:33,649 --> 00:03:37,130
A perhaps uncalled for gush of pity came over my heart.

52
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:43,289
I was moved to say, I wished Diana or Mary would come and live with you.

53
00:03:43,990 --> 00:03:47,354
It is too bad that you should be quite alone, and

54
00:03:47,355 --> 00:03:50,311
you are recklessly rash about your own health.

55
00:03:51,289 --> 00:03:53,050
Not at all, said he.

56
00:03:53,051 --> 00:03:56,970
I care for myself when necessary, I am well now.

57
00:03:57,130 --> 00:03:58,669
What do you see amiss in me?

58
00:03:59,809 --> 00:04:04,889
This was said with a careless, abstracted indifference, which showed that

59
00:04:04,891 --> 00:04:10,050
my solicitude was, at least in his opinion, wholly superfluous.

60
00:04:10,729 --> 00:04:12,130
I was silenced.

61
00:04:13,009 --> 00:04:19,229
He still slowly moved his finger over his upper lip and still his eye dwelt dreamily

62
00:04:19,230 --> 00:04:23,070
on the glowing grate, thinking it urgent to say something.

63
00:04:23,809 --> 00:04:29,031
I asked him presently if he felt any cold draught from the door which was behind him.

64
00:04:29,210 --> 00:04:32,509
No, no, he responded shortly and somewhat testily.

65
00:04:33,350 --> 00:04:37,750
Well, I reflected, if you won't talk, you may be still.

66
00:04:38,770 --> 00:04:41,809
I'll let you alone now, and return to my book.

67
00:04:42,669 --> 00:04:45,830
So I snuffed the candle and resumed the perusal of Marmian.

68
00:04:46,929 --> 00:04:47,929
He soon stirred.

69
00:04:48,750 --> 00:04:51,210
My eye was instantly drawn to his movements.

70
00:04:51,789 --> 00:04:57,770
He only took out a Morocco pocketbook, then produced a letter, which he read in

71
00:04:57,770 --> 00:05:02,889
silence, folded it, put it back, relapsed into meditation.

72
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:08,429
It was vain to try to read with such an inscrutable fixture before me,

73
00:05:09,190 --> 00:05:12,630
nor could I, in impatience, consent to be dumb.

74
00:05:13,669 --> 00:05:17,210
He might rebuff me if he liked, but talk I would.

75
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:21,190
Have you heard from Diana and Mary lately?

76
00:05:22,750 --> 00:05:24,789
Not since the letter I showed you a week ago.

77
00:05:25,990 --> 00:05:29,070
There has not been any change made about your own arrangements.

78
00:05:29,970 --> 00:05:33,089
You will not be summoned to leave England sooner than you expected.

79
00:05:34,050 --> 00:05:35,910
I fear not, indeed.

80
00:05:36,729 --> 00:05:39,080
Such chance is too good to fall me.

81
00:05:40,559 --> 00:05:43,220
Baffled so far, I changed my ground.

82
00:05:44,339 --> 00:05:47,559
I bethought myself to talk about the school and my scholars.

83
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:53,039
Mary Garrett's mother is better, and Mary came back to the school this

84
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:57,399
morning, and I shall have four new girls next week from the foundry clothes.

85
00:05:58,380 --> 00:06:00,279
They would have come today, but for the snow.

86
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:04,059
Indeed, Mr. Oliver pays for two.

87
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:06,080
Does he?

88
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:08,580
He means to give the whole school a treat at Christmas.

89
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,440
I know.

90
00:06:10,679 --> 00:06:11,699
Was it your suggestion?

91
00:06:12,660 --> 00:06:13,660
No.

92
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:14,800
Who's then?

93
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:16,600
His daughters, I think.

94
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,580
It is like her.

95
00:06:19,259 --> 00:06:20,639
She is so good-natured.

96
00:06:21,399 --> 00:06:24,820
Yes, again came the blank of a pause.

97
00:06:25,660 --> 00:06:27,679
The clock struck eight strokes.

98
00:06:28,539 --> 00:06:29,539
It aroused him.

99
00:06:30,139 --> 00:06:34,179
He uncrossed his legs, sat erect, turned to me.

100
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:40,440
And leave your book a moment, and come a little nearer the fire, he said.

101
00:06:41,479 --> 00:06:45,839
Wondering, and of my wonder finding no end, I complied.

102
00:06:47,220 --> 00:06:49,580
Half an hour ago, he pursued.

103
00:06:50,639 --> 00:06:53,759
I spoke of my impatience to hear the sequel of a tale.

104
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:59,199
On reflection, I find the matter will be better managed by my assuming the

105
00:06:59,201 --> 00:07:02,880
narrator's part, and converting you into a listener.

106
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:09,479
Before commencing, it is but fair to warn you that the story will sound somewhat

107
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:14,730
hackneyed in your ears, but stale details often regain

108
00:07:14,732 --> 00:07:18,399
a degree of freshness when they pass through new lips.

109
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:22,520
For the rest, whether trite or novel, it is short.

110
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:28,758
20 years ago, a poor curate, never find his name at

111
00:07:28,759 --> 00:07:32,300
this moment, fell in love with a rich man's daughter.

112
00:07:33,179 --> 00:07:37,860
She fell in love with him and married him, against the advice of all her friends,

113
00:07:38,360 --> 00:07:41,960
who consequently disowned her immediately after the wedding.

114
00:07:43,119 --> 00:07:46,948
Before two years passed, the rash pair were both

115
00:07:46,948 --> 00:07:51,160
dead and laid quietly side by side under one slab.

116
00:07:52,259 --> 00:07:53,820
I have seen their grave.

117
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:58,539
It formed part of the pavement of a huge churchyard surrounding the grim,

118
00:07:59,119 --> 00:08:04,639
sut black old cathedral of an overgrown manufacturing town in Shire.

119
00:08:05,399 --> 00:08:11,300
They left a daughter, which, at its very birth, charity received in her lap,

120
00:08:12,339 --> 00:08:16,940
cold as that of the snowdrift I almost stuck fast in tonight.

121
00:08:18,479 --> 00:08:22,820
Charity carried the friendless thing to the house of its rich maternal relations.

122
00:08:23,639 --> 00:08:28,619
It was reared by an aunt-in-law, called, I come to names now, Mrs.

123
00:08:28,619 --> 00:08:30,240
Reed of Gateshead.

124
00:08:30,479 --> 00:08:31,479
You start.

125
00:08:32,259 --> 00:08:33,259
Did you hear a noise?

126
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:39,980
I dare say it is only a rat scrambling along the rafters of the adjoining schoolroom.

127
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:42,756
It was a barn before I had it repaired and

128
00:08:42,758 --> 00:08:46,421
altered, and barns are generally haunted by rats.

129
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:47,940
To proceed.

130
00:08:48,919 --> 00:08:53,860
Mrs. Reed kept the orphan ten years, whether it was happy or not with her,

131
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:57,020
I cannot say, never having been told.

132
00:08:57,979 --> 00:09:01,419
But at the end of that time she transferred it to a place you know,

133
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:07,039
being no other than lowered school, where you so long resided yourself.

134
00:09:08,479 --> 00:09:11,580
It seems her career there was very honourable.

135
00:09:12,059 --> 00:09:15,320
From a pupil she became a teacher like yourself.

136
00:09:16,559 --> 00:09:21,320
Really, it strikes me there are parallel points in her history and yours.

137
00:09:22,479 --> 00:09:23,979
She left it to be a governess.

138
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:27,940
There again, your fates were analogous.

139
00:09:28,699 --> 00:09:32,419
She undertook the education of the ward of a certain Mr. Rochester.

140
00:09:33,919 --> 00:09:35,899
Mr. Rivers, I interrupted.

141
00:09:36,339 --> 00:09:40,600
I can guess your feelings, he said, but restrain them for a while.

142
00:09:41,279 --> 00:09:42,639
I have nearly finished.

143
00:09:43,300 --> 00:09:44,300
Hear me to the end.

144
00:09:45,179 --> 00:09:51,919
Of Mr. Rochester's character, I know nothing, but the one fact that he

145
00:09:51,921 --> 00:09:57,580
professed to offer honourable marriage to this young girl, and that at the very

146
00:09:57,581 --> 00:10:01,600
altar she discovered he had a wife, yet alive.

147
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:08,880
Though a lunatic, what his subsequent conduct and proposals were is a matter of

148
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:14,259
pure conjecture, but when an event transpired, which rendered inquiry after

149
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:19,899
the governess necessary, it was discovered she was gone, no one could tell when,

150
00:10:20,199 --> 00:10:21,320
where or how.

151
00:10:23,059 --> 00:10:25,919
She had left Thornfield Hall in the night.

152
00:10:26,860 --> 00:10:31,759
Every research after her course had been vain, the country had been scoured far and

153
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:35,800
wide, no vestige of information could be gathered respecting her.

154
00:10:37,199 --> 00:10:42,960
Yet, that she should be found, is become a matter of serious urgency.

155
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:46,360
Advertisements have been put in all the papers.

156
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:51,294
I myself have received a letter from one Mr. Briggs, a

157
00:10:51,296 --> 00:10:55,580
solicitor, communicating the details I have just imparted.

158
00:10:55,979 --> 00:10:57,360
Is it not an odd tale?

159
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:04,699
Just tell me this, said I, and since you know so much, you surely can tell it me,

160
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:06,160
what of Mr. Rochester?

161
00:11:06,899 --> 00:11:07,979
How and where is he?

162
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:09,520
What is he doing?

163
00:11:09,899 --> 00:11:10,899
Is he well?

164
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:15,300
I am ignorant of all concerning Mr. Rochester.

165
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:19,529
The letter never mentions him, but to narrate the

166
00:11:19,531 --> 00:11:23,020
fraudulent and illegal attempt I have adverted to.

167
00:11:23,860 --> 00:11:27,154
You should rather ask the name of the governess, the

168
00:11:27,156 --> 00:11:30,199
nature of the event which requires her appearance.

169
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:33,919
Did no one go to Thornfield Hall then?

170
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,300
Did no one see Mr. Rochester?

171
00:11:37,539 --> 00:11:38,539
I suppose not.

172
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:41,940
But they wrote to him, of course.

173
00:11:42,820 --> 00:11:43,960
And what did he say?

174
00:11:44,779 --> 00:11:45,779
Who has his letters?

175
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:50,600
Mr. Briggs intimates that the answer to his application was not from Mr.

176
00:11:50,660 --> 00:11:52,500
Rochester, but from a lady.

177
00:11:53,339 --> 00:11:55,600
It is signed Alice Fairfax.

178
00:11:57,940 --> 00:12:00,360
I felt cold and dismayed.

179
00:12:01,660 --> 00:12:03,779
My worst fears then were probably true.

180
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,857
He had in all probability left England and rushed in

181
00:12:07,857 --> 00:12:10,699
reckless desperation to some former haunt on the continent.

182
00:12:11,399 --> 00:12:13,880
And what opiate for his severe sufferings?

183
00:12:14,320 --> 00:12:16,440
What object for his strong passions?

184
00:12:17,119 --> 00:12:18,119
Had he sought there?

185
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:21,639
I dared not answer the question.

186
00:12:22,679 --> 00:12:23,899
Oh, my poor master.

187
00:12:24,919 --> 00:12:29,134
Once almost my husband, whom I had often called my dear

188
00:12:29,134 --> 00:12:33,259
Edward, he must have been a bad man observed Mr. Rivers.

189
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:35,800
You don't know him.

190
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:39,240
Don't pronounce an opinion upon him, I said, with warmth.

191
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:42,500
Very well, he answered quietly.

192
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:46,619
And indeed, my head is otherwise occupied than with him.

193
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:49,520
I have my tail to finish.

194
00:12:50,619 --> 00:12:55,399
Since you won't ask the governess's name, I must tell it of my own accord.

195
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:57,600
Stay.

196
00:12:57,899 --> 00:12:58,899
I have it here.

197
00:12:59,539 --> 00:13:02,919
It is always more satisfactory to see important points written down,

198
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:05,380
fairly committed to black and white.

199
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:12,360
And, the pocketbook was again deliberately produced, opened, sought through.

200
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:18,800
From one of its compartments was extracted a shabby slip of paper hastily torn off.

201
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:23,941
I recognized in its texture and its stains of ultra-marine and

202
00:13:23,942 --> 00:13:27,580
lake and vermilion the ravished margin of the portrait cover.

203
00:13:28,339 --> 00:13:34,979
He got up, held it close to my eyes, and I read, traced in Indian ink in my own

204
00:13:34,980 --> 00:13:42,540
hand writing, the words Jane Eyre, the work, doubtless of some moment of abstraction.

205
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:47,100
Briggs wrote to me of a Jane Eyre, he said.

206
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:50,419
The advertisements demanded a Jane Eyre.

207
00:13:50,699 --> 00:13:51,919
I knew a Jane Elliott.

208
00:13:52,559 --> 00:13:55,884
I confess I had my suspicions, but it was only yesterday

209
00:13:55,885 --> 00:13:58,539
afternoon they were at once resolved into certainty.

210
00:13:59,259 --> 00:14:01,539
You own the name and renounce the alias.

211
00:14:02,779 --> 00:14:05,460
Yes, yes, but where is Mr. Briggs?

212
00:14:05,820 --> 00:14:08,500
He perhaps knows more of Mr. Rochester than you do.

213
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,039
Briggs is in London.

214
00:14:13,259 --> 00:14:16,080
I should doubt his knowing anything at all about Mr. Rochester.

215
00:14:16,740 --> 00:14:19,479
It is not in Mr. Rochester he is interested.

216
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:24,880
Meantime, you forget essential points in pursuing trifles.

217
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:28,619
You do not inquire why Mr. Briggs sought after you.

218
00:14:29,179 --> 00:14:30,580
What he wanted with you.

219
00:14:31,440 --> 00:14:33,220
Well, what did he want?

220
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:40,339
Mealy to tell you that your uncle, Mr. Eyre of Madira, is dead, that he has

221
00:14:40,341 --> 00:14:45,479
left you all his property, and that you are now rich, merely that, nothing more.

222
00:14:46,619 --> 00:14:51,419
I, rich, yes, you rich, quite an heiress.

223
00:14:52,220 --> 00:14:53,279
Silence succeeded.

224
00:14:54,660 --> 00:14:57,039
You must prove your identity, of course.

225
00:14:58,160 --> 00:14:59,779
Resumed singeon presently.

226
00:15:00,259 --> 00:15:05,361
A step which will offer no difficulties, you can then enter on immediate possession.

227
00:15:05,759 --> 00:15:08,399
Your fortune is vested in the English funds.

228
00:15:08,899 --> 00:15:11,320
Briggs has the will and the necessary documents.

229
00:15:12,979 --> 00:15:15,259
Here was a new card turned up.

230
00:15:15,899 --> 00:15:20,639
It is a fine thing, reader, to be lifted in a moment from indigence to wealth,

231
00:15:21,399 --> 00:15:24,498
a very fine thing, but not a matter one can

232
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:28,361
comprehend or consequently enjoy all at once.

233
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:33,500
And then, there are other chances in life far more thrilling and rapture giving.

234
00:15:34,199 --> 00:15:39,539
This is solid, an affair of the actual world, nothing ideal about it.

235
00:15:40,020 --> 00:15:44,820
All its associations are solid and sober, and its manifestations are the same.

236
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:48,460
One does not jump and spring and shout hurrah.

237
00:15:49,759 --> 00:15:52,039
At hearing one has got a fortune.

238
00:15:52,880 --> 00:15:56,059
One begins to consider responsibilities and to ponder business.

239
00:15:57,100 --> 00:16:02,419
On a base of steady satisfaction rise certain grave cares, and we contain

240
00:16:02,421 --> 00:16:05,660
ourselves and brood over our bliss with a solemn brow.

241
00:16:06,539 --> 00:16:13,339
Besides the words legacy, bequest, go side by side with the words death funeral.

242
00:16:14,580 --> 00:16:16,419
My uncle I had heard was dead.

243
00:16:17,139 --> 00:16:18,139
My only relative.

244
00:16:19,059 --> 00:16:21,442
Ever since being made aware of his existence,

245
00:16:21,444 --> 00:16:24,339
I had cherished the hope of one day seeing him.

246
00:16:25,039 --> 00:16:27,119
Now, I never should.

247
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:32,380
And then this money came only to me, not to me and a rejoicing family,

248
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:34,839
but to my isolated self.

249
00:16:35,440 --> 00:16:39,660
It was a grand boon doubtless, and independence would be glorious.

250
00:16:40,039 --> 00:16:41,039
Yes, I felt that.

251
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:43,259
That thought swelled my heart.

252
00:16:44,699 --> 00:16:48,000
You unbend your forehead at last, said Mr. Rivers.

253
00:16:49,039 --> 00:16:52,479
I thought Medusa had looked at you, and that you were turning to stone.

254
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:56,639
Perhaps now, you will ask how much you are worth.

255
00:16:57,639 --> 00:16:59,139
How much am I worth?

256
00:17:00,059 --> 00:17:01,199
Oh, a trifle.

257
00:17:01,699 --> 00:17:02,979
Nothing, of course, to speak of.

258
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,559
20,000 pounds, I think they say.

259
00:17:06,080 --> 00:17:07,160
But what is that?

260
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,600
20,000 pounds.

261
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,880
Here was a new stunner.

262
00:17:13,600 --> 00:17:15,779
I had been calculating on four or five thousand.

263
00:17:16,679 --> 00:17:18,720
This news actually took my breath for a moment.

264
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:23,740
Mr. Singen, whom I had never heard laugh before, laughed now.

265
00:17:25,360 --> 00:17:26,759
Well, said he.

266
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:31,399
If you had committed a murder, and I had told you your crime was

267
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:34,679
discovered, you could scarcely look more aghast.

268
00:17:35,660 --> 00:17:37,300
It is a large sum.

269
00:17:37,860 --> 00:17:39,259
Don't you think there is a mistake?

270
00:17:40,080 --> 00:17:41,160
No mistake at all.

271
00:17:42,119 --> 00:17:43,720
Perhaps you have read the figures wrong.

272
00:17:44,479 --> 00:17:45,500
It may be two thousand.

273
00:17:46,479 --> 00:17:49,360
It is written in letters, not figures.

274
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,320
20,000.

275
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:57,539
I again felt rather like an individual of but average gastronomical powers sitting

276
00:17:57,540 --> 00:18:02,080
down to feast alone at a table spread with provisions for a hundred.

277
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:06,619
Mr. Rivers rose now and put his cloak on.

278
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:11,399
If it were not such a very wild night, he said,

279
00:18:11,399 --> 00:18:14,801
I would send Hannah down to keep you company.

280
00:18:15,179 --> 00:18:17,720
You look too desperately miserable to be left alone.

281
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:23,440
But Hannah, poor woman, could not stride the drift so well as I.

282
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:29,119
Her legs are not quite so long, so I must in leave you to your sorrows.

283
00:18:29,979 --> 00:18:30,979
Good night.

284
00:18:31,940 --> 00:18:33,080
He was lifting the latch.

285
00:18:33,919 --> 00:18:35,399
A sudden thought occurred to me.

286
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:37,380
Stop one minute, I cried.

287
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:44,919
Well, it puzzles me to know why Mr. Briggs wrote to you about me, or how he knew you,

288
00:18:45,559 --> 00:18:48,683
or could fancy that you, living in such an out of

289
00:18:48,684 --> 00:18:51,900
the way place, had the power to aid in my discovery.

290
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:56,357
Oh, I am a clergyman, he said, and the clergy

291
00:18:56,357 --> 00:18:59,520
are often appealed to about odd matters.

292
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,160
Again, the latch rattled.

293
00:19:03,220 --> 00:19:06,179
No, that does not satisfy me, I exclaimed.

294
00:19:07,300 --> 00:19:12,860
And indeed, there was something in the hasty and unexplanatory reply which,

295
00:19:13,199 --> 00:19:16,860
instead of a laying peaked my curiosity more than ever.

296
00:19:17,559 --> 00:19:20,600
It is a very strange piece of business, I added.

297
00:19:21,119 --> 00:19:22,580
I must know more about it.

298
00:19:23,619 --> 00:19:24,619
Another time.

299
00:19:25,679 --> 00:19:28,100
No, tonight, tonight.

300
00:19:29,539 --> 00:19:35,440
And as he turned from the door, I placed myself between it and him.

301
00:19:36,660 --> 00:19:38,119
He looked rather embarrassed.

302
00:19:39,699 --> 00:19:43,440
You certainly shall not go till you have told me all, I said.

303
00:19:44,500 --> 00:19:49,339
I would rather not just now, you shall, you must.

304
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:53,240
I would rather Diana or Mary informed you.

305
00:19:53,979 --> 00:19:59,399
Of course, these objections brought my eagerness to a climax, gratified it must

306
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:02,679
be, and that without delay, and I told him so.

307
00:20:03,580 --> 00:20:08,779
But I apprised you that I was a hard man, said he, difficult to persuade.

308
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:13,119
And I am a hard woman, impossible to put off.

309
00:20:13,619 --> 00:20:18,059
And then he pursued, I am cold, no further infects me.

310
00:20:18,979 --> 00:20:23,152
Whereas I am hot, and fire dissolves ice, the blaze

311
00:20:23,153 --> 00:20:26,400
there has thawed all the snow from your cloak.

312
00:20:27,380 --> 00:20:33,839
By the same token, it has streamed onto my floor and made it like a trampled street.

313
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:40,740
As you hope ever to be forgiven, Mr Rivers, the high crime and misdemeanor

314
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:45,039
of spoiling a sanded kitchen, tell me what I wish to know.

315
00:20:46,279 --> 00:20:52,000
Well then, he said, I yield, if not to your earnestness to your perseverance,

316
00:20:52,660 --> 00:20:57,779
as stone is worn by continual dropping, besides, you must know someday,

317
00:20:58,440 --> 00:20:59,639
as well now as later.

318
00:21:00,559 --> 00:21:01,820
Your name is Jane Eyre?

319
00:21:02,399 --> 00:21:05,300
Of course, that was all settled before.

320
00:21:06,619 --> 00:21:09,216
You are not, perhaps, aware that I am your

321
00:21:09,217 --> 00:21:12,721
namesake, that I was christened Syngin Eyre Rivers?

322
00:21:13,539 --> 00:21:14,860
No, indeed.

323
00:21:15,880 --> 00:21:21,520
I remember now seeing the letter E, comprised in your initials, written in

324
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:24,179
books, you have at different times lent me.

325
00:21:24,919 --> 00:21:32,479
But I never asked for what name it stood, but what then, surely, I stopped.

326
00:21:33,300 --> 00:21:38,360
I could not trust myself to entertain, much less to express, the thought that

327
00:21:38,361 --> 00:21:42,282
rushed upon me, that embodied itself, that in

328
00:21:42,283 --> 00:21:46,120
a second stood out a strong solid probability.

329
00:21:47,500 --> 00:21:52,500
Circumstances knit themselves, fitted themselves, shot into order.

330
00:21:53,500 --> 00:21:55,664
The chain that had been lying hitherto a

331
00:21:55,664 --> 00:21:58,960
formless lump of links was drawn out straight.

332
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:02,520
Every ring was perfect, the connection complete.

333
00:22:03,259 --> 00:22:09,520
I knew, by instinct, how the matter stood, before Syngin had said another word,

334
00:22:10,339 --> 00:22:13,220
but I cannot expect the reader to have the same

335
00:22:13,221 --> 00:22:16,839
intuitive perception, so I must repeat his explanation.

336
00:22:18,339 --> 00:22:20,160
My mother's name was Eyre.

337
00:22:20,600 --> 00:22:25,860
She had two brothers, one a clergyman, who married Miss Jane Reed of Gateshead,

338
00:22:26,360 --> 00:22:31,460
the other, John Eyre ESQ, merchant, late of Funchal Madera.

339
00:22:32,320 --> 00:22:38,020
Mr. Briggs, being Mr. Eyre's solicitor, wrote to us last August, to inform us of

340
00:22:38,020 --> 00:22:43,300
our uncle's death, and to say that he had left his property to his brother,

341
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:49,000
the clergyman's orphan daughter, overlooking us, in consequence of a

342
00:22:49,001 --> 00:22:53,139
quarrel, never forgiven, between him and my father.

343
00:22:53,860 --> 00:22:58,080
He wrote again a few weeks since, to intimate that the ares was lost,

344
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:00,839
and asking if we knew anything of her.

345
00:23:01,679 --> 00:23:05,699
A name casually written on a slip of paper has enabled me to find her out.

346
00:23:06,699 --> 00:23:07,699
You know the rest.

347
00:23:09,020 --> 00:23:11,899
Again, he was going, but I set my back against the door.

348
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:14,580
Do let me speak, I said.

349
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:17,460
Let me have one moment to draw breath and reflect.

350
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:19,500
I paused.

351
00:23:19,800 --> 00:23:23,240
He stood before me, hat in hand, looking composed enough.

352
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:24,399
I resumed.

353
00:23:24,860 --> 00:23:26,259
Your mother was my father's sister?

354
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:27,960
Yes.

355
00:23:28,179 --> 00:23:30,619
My aunt, consequently, he bowed.

356
00:23:31,440 --> 00:23:33,380
My uncle John was your uncle John.

357
00:23:34,479 --> 00:23:39,399
You, Diana, and Mary are his sister's children, as I am his brother's child,

358
00:23:40,199 --> 00:23:41,199
undeniably.

359
00:23:41,860 --> 00:23:43,259
You three then are my cousins.

360
00:23:44,220 --> 00:23:47,440
Half our blood on each side flows from the same source.

361
00:23:49,339 --> 00:23:50,820
We are cousins, yes.

362
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:53,220
I surveyed him.

363
00:23:53,899 --> 00:23:55,179
It seemed I had found a brother.

364
00:23:55,839 --> 00:24:01,860
One I could be proud of, one I could love, and two sisters, whose qualities were

365
00:24:01,861 --> 00:24:07,051
such, that when I knew them, but as mere strangers, they

366
00:24:07,052 --> 00:24:11,080
had inspired me with genuine affection and admiration.

367
00:24:12,139 --> 00:24:18,320
The two girls, on whom, kneeling down on the wet ground, and looking through the

368
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:24,240
low, lattice window of Morehouse Kitchen, I had gazed with so bitter a mixture of

369
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:30,020
interest and despair, were my near-kins' women, and the young and stately

370
00:24:30,020 --> 00:24:35,580
gentleman, who had found me almost dying at his threshold, was my blood relation,

371
00:24:36,520 --> 00:24:39,199
glorious discovery to a lonely wretch.

372
00:24:39,979 --> 00:24:45,860
This was wealth in deed, wealth to the heart, a mine of pure genial affections.

373
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:52,399
This was a blessing, bright, vivid, and exhilarating, not like the ponderous

374
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:57,639
gift of gold, rich and welcome enough in its way, but sobering from its weight.

375
00:24:58,600 --> 00:25:03,020
I now clapped my hands in sudden joy, my pulse bounded, my veins thrilled.

376
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:04,600
Oh, I am glad!

377
00:25:05,139 --> 00:25:08,619
I am glad!" I exclaimed, Syngin smiled.

378
00:25:10,080 --> 00:25:13,699
Did I not say you neglected essential points to pursue trifles?

379
00:25:14,380 --> 00:25:15,380
He asked.

380
00:25:15,820 --> 00:25:19,225
You were serious when I told you you'd got a fortune,

381
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:22,600
and now, for a matter of no moment, you are excited.

382
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:24,880
What can you mean?

383
00:25:26,240 --> 00:25:27,720
It may be of no moment to you.

384
00:25:28,559 --> 00:25:32,039
You have sisters and don't care for a cousin, but I had nobody.

385
00:25:32,860 --> 00:25:36,137
And now, three relations, or two if you don't choose

386
00:25:36,138 --> 00:25:39,619
to be counted, are born into my world full grown.

387
00:25:40,619 --> 00:25:42,759
I say again, I am glad.

388
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:46,100
I walked fast through the room.

389
00:25:47,339 --> 00:25:50,298
I stopped, half suffocated with the thoughts that rose

390
00:25:50,300 --> 00:25:54,759
faster than I could receive, comprehend, settle them.

391
00:25:55,940 --> 00:26:00,960
Thoughts of what might, could, would, and should be, and that air long.

392
00:26:01,979 --> 00:26:03,500
I looked at the blank wall.

393
00:26:04,339 --> 00:26:06,580
It seemed a sky thick with ascending stars.

394
00:26:07,419 --> 00:26:09,320
Everyone lit me to a purpose or delight.

395
00:26:10,360 --> 00:26:14,580
Those who had saved my life, whom, till this hour I had loved apparently,

396
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:16,020
I could now benefit.

397
00:26:16,759 --> 00:26:18,199
They were under a yoke.

398
00:26:18,779 --> 00:26:19,779
I could free them.

399
00:26:20,100 --> 00:26:21,100
They were scattered.

400
00:26:21,199 --> 00:26:22,240
I could reunite them.

401
00:26:23,139 --> 00:26:28,179
The independence, the affluence, which was mine, might be theirs, too.

402
00:26:28,500 --> 00:26:29,500
Were we not full?

403
00:26:29,979 --> 00:26:33,720
20,000 pounds shared equally would be 5 ,000 each.

404
00:26:34,179 --> 00:26:35,179
Justice.

405
00:26:35,460 --> 00:26:36,639
Enough and to spare.

406
00:26:37,380 --> 00:26:38,380
Justice would be done.

407
00:26:39,100 --> 00:26:40,520
Mutual happiness secured.

408
00:26:41,880 --> 00:26:43,580
Now the wealth did not weigh on me.

409
00:26:44,020 --> 00:26:46,460
Now it was not a mere bequest of coin.

410
00:26:47,179 --> 00:26:50,279
It was a legacy of life, hope, enjoyment.

411
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:56,160
How I looked while these ideas were taking my spirit by storm, I cannot tell.

412
00:26:57,520 --> 00:27:02,085
But I perceived soon that Mr. Rivers had placed a chair

413
00:27:02,085 --> 00:27:05,779
behind me and was gently attempting to make me sit down on it.

414
00:27:06,779 --> 00:27:08,940
He also advised me to be composed.

415
00:27:10,279 --> 00:27:13,820
I scorned the insinuation of helplessness and distraction.

416
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:18,039
Shook off his hand and began to walk about again.

417
00:27:19,160 --> 00:27:25,061
Write to Diana and Mary tomorrow, I said, and tell them to come home directly.

418
00:27:25,740 --> 00:27:29,800
Diana said they would both consider themselves rich with a thousand pounds,

419
00:27:30,520 --> 00:27:33,080
so with 5,000 they will do very well.

420
00:27:34,580 --> 00:27:38,539
Tell me where I can get you a glass of water, said Sinjin.

421
00:27:39,419 --> 00:27:42,539
You must really make an effort to tranquilise your feelings.

422
00:27:43,679 --> 00:27:44,679
Nonsense.

423
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:48,139
And what sort of an effect will the bequest have on you?

424
00:27:48,880 --> 00:27:50,000
Will it keep you in England?

425
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:54,539
Induce you to marry Miss Oliver and settle down like an ordinary mortal?

426
00:27:56,259 --> 00:27:59,639
You wonder, your head becomes confused.

427
00:28:00,639 --> 00:28:03,559
I have been too abrupt in communicating the news.

428
00:28:09,520 --> 00:28:11,059
It has made me out of patience.

429
00:28:11,919 --> 00:28:13,160
I am rational enough.

430
00:28:14,080 --> 00:28:18,520
It is you who misunderstand, or rather who affect to misunderstand.

431
00:28:19,479 --> 00:28:24,139
Perhaps, if you explain yourself a little more fully, I should comprehend better.

432
00:28:25,779 --> 00:28:26,779
Explain.

433
00:28:27,419 --> 00:28:29,059
What is there to explain?

434
00:28:30,380 --> 00:28:36,860
You cannot fail to see that 20,000 pounds, the sum in question, divided equally

435
00:28:36,861 --> 00:28:41,880
between the nephew and three nieces of our uncle, will give 5,000 to each?

436
00:28:42,580 --> 00:28:45,486
What I want is that you should write to your sisters

437
00:28:45,487 --> 00:28:48,139
and tell them of the fortune that has accrued to them.

438
00:28:49,380 --> 00:28:50,380
To you, you mean.

439
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:54,100
I have intimated my view of the case.

440
00:28:55,279 --> 00:28:57,160
I am incapable of taking any other.

441
00:28:57,960 --> 00:29:03,639
I am not brutally selfish, blindly unjust, or fiendishly ungrateful.

442
00:29:04,440 --> 00:29:08,300
Besides, I am resolved I will have a home and connections.

443
00:29:09,240 --> 00:29:12,479
I like more house, and I will live at more house.

444
00:29:12,960 --> 00:29:18,259
I like Diana and Mary, and I will attach myself a life to Diana and Mary.

445
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:22,059
It would please and benefit me to have 5 ,000 pounds.

446
00:29:22,779 --> 00:29:27,589
It would torment and oppress me to have 20 ,000, which moreover

447
00:29:27,591 --> 00:29:31,720
could never be mine in justice, though it might in law.

448
00:29:33,039 --> 00:29:37,779
I abandoned to you, then, what is absolutely superfluous to me.

449
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,979
Let there be no opposition and no discussion about it.

450
00:29:42,679 --> 00:29:46,380
Let us agree amongst each other and decide the point at once.

451
00:29:47,660 --> 00:29:50,080
This is acting on first impulses.

452
00:29:50,679 --> 00:29:52,919
You must take days to consider such a matter.

453
00:29:53,520 --> 00:29:55,600
Your word can be regarded as valid.

454
00:29:56,639 --> 00:30:01,800
Oh, if all you doubt is my sincerity, I am easy.

455
00:30:02,279 --> 00:30:03,559
You see the justice of the case?

456
00:30:04,559 --> 00:30:08,919
I do see a certain justice, but it is contrary to all custom.

457
00:30:09,779 --> 00:30:12,800
Besides, the entire fortune is your right.

458
00:30:13,539 --> 00:30:15,440
My uncle gained it by his own efforts.

459
00:30:16,360 --> 00:30:18,679
He was free to leave it to whom he would.

460
00:30:19,460 --> 00:30:20,460
He left it to you.

461
00:30:21,100 --> 00:30:24,240
After all, justice permits you to keep it.

462
00:30:24,899 --> 00:30:29,779
You may, with a clear conscience, consider it absolutely your own.

463
00:30:31,039 --> 00:30:35,520
With me, said I, it is fully as much a matter of feeling as of conscience.

464
00:30:36,539 --> 00:30:37,940
I must indulge my feelings.

465
00:30:38,820 --> 00:30:41,779
I so seldom have had an opportunity of doing so.

466
00:30:42,539 --> 00:30:47,039
Were you to argue, object, and annoy me for a year?

467
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:51,759
I could not forego the delicious pleasure of which I have quarter-glimps,

468
00:30:52,580 --> 00:30:55,789
that of repaying, in part, a mighty obligation,

469
00:30:55,790 --> 00:30:59,081
and winning to myself lifelong friends?

470
00:31:00,580 --> 00:31:02,160
You think so now?

471
00:31:02,960 --> 00:31:06,139
Rejoin, Sinjin, because you do not know what it

472
00:31:06,141 --> 00:31:09,501
is to possess, nor consequently to enjoy wealth.

473
00:31:10,279 --> 00:31:16,160
You cannot form a notion of the importance 20,000 pounds would give you, of the place

474
00:31:16,160 --> 00:31:21,080
it would enable you to take in society, of the prospects it would open to you,

475
00:31:21,199 --> 00:31:22,199
you cannot.

476
00:31:22,539 --> 00:31:26,634
And you, I interrupted, cannot at all imagine the

477
00:31:26,635 --> 00:31:30,059
craving I have for fraternal and sisterly love.

478
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:32,259
I never had a home.

479
00:31:32,960 --> 00:31:34,240
I never had brothers or sisters.

480
00:31:34,660 --> 00:31:36,339
I must and will have them now.

481
00:31:36,759 --> 00:31:40,199
You are not reluctant to admit me and own me, are you?

482
00:31:41,339 --> 00:31:43,339
Jane, I will be your brother.

483
00:31:44,100 --> 00:31:46,461
My sisters will be your sisters, without

484
00:31:46,463 --> 00:31:49,400
stipulating for this sacrifice of your just rights.

485
00:31:50,139 --> 00:31:55,619
Brother, yes, at the distance of a thousand leagues, sisters, yes,

486
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:57,479
slaving among strangers.

487
00:31:58,440 --> 00:32:03,440
I, wealthy, gorged with gold, I never earned and do not merit.

488
00:32:03,960 --> 00:32:11,480
You, penniless, famous equality and fraternization, close union, intimate attachment.

489
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:19,100
But Jane, your aspirations after family ties and domestic happiness may be

490
00:32:19,100 --> 00:32:22,919
realized otherwise than by the means you contemplate.

491
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:25,000
You may marry.

492
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:27,639
Nonsense again, marry.

493
00:32:28,220 --> 00:32:30,660
I don't want to marry and never shall marry.

494
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:33,020
That is saying too much.

495
00:32:33,619 --> 00:32:38,339
Such hazardous affirmations are a proof of the excitement under which you labor.

496
00:32:39,899 --> 00:32:41,639
It is not saying too much.

497
00:32:42,460 --> 00:32:44,754
I know what I feel and how averse are my

498
00:32:44,755 --> 00:32:48,081
inclinations to the bare thought of marriage.

499
00:32:48,320 --> 00:32:49,619
No one would take me for love.

500
00:32:50,720 --> 00:32:54,199
And I will not be regarded in the light of a mere money speculation.

501
00:32:54,940 --> 00:33:00,479
And I do not want a stranger unsympathizing alien different from me.

502
00:33:00,899 --> 00:33:05,619
I want my kindred, those with whom I have full fellow feeling.

503
00:33:06,960 --> 00:33:09,279
Say again, you will be my brother.

504
00:33:10,139 --> 00:33:12,979
When you uttered the words, I was satisfied, happy.

505
00:33:13,660 --> 00:33:14,779
Repeat them if you can.

506
00:33:15,619 --> 00:33:16,919
Repeat them sincerely.

507
00:33:18,679 --> 00:33:19,880
I think I can.

508
00:33:20,800 --> 00:33:26,559
I know I have always loved my own sisters, and I know on what my affection for them

509
00:33:26,561 --> 00:33:30,539
is grounded, respect for their worth and admiration of their talents.

510
00:33:32,100 --> 00:33:38,100
You too have principle and mind, your tastes and habits resemble dinners and marries.

511
00:33:38,639 --> 00:33:40,979
Your presence is always agreeable to me.

512
00:33:41,899 --> 00:33:47,320
In your conversation, I have already for some time found a salutary solace.

513
00:33:48,259 --> 00:33:52,225
I feel I can easily and naturally make room in

514
00:33:52,226 --> 00:33:56,179
my heart for you as my third and youngest sister.

515
00:33:57,500 --> 00:33:58,500
Thank you.

516
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:00,320
That contends me for tonight.

517
00:34:01,279 --> 00:34:04,131
Now you had better go, for if you stay longer, you will

518
00:34:04,133 --> 00:34:07,039
perhaps irritate me afresh by some mistrustful scruple.

519
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:12,279
And the school, miss air, it must now be shut up, I suppose.

520
00:34:13,559 --> 00:34:18,380
No, I will retain my post of mistrust till you get a substitute.

521
00:34:19,119 --> 00:34:23,419
He smiled at probation, we shook hands and he took leave.

522
00:34:25,220 --> 00:34:31,119
I need not narrate in detail the further struggles I had and arguments I used to

523
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:34,119
get matters regarding the legacy settled as I wished.

524
00:34:35,419 --> 00:34:42,419
My task was a very hard one, but as I was absolutely resolved, as my cousin saw at

525
00:34:42,421 --> 00:34:46,460
length that my mind was really an immutably fixed on making a just division

526
00:34:46,460 --> 00:34:50,940
of the property, as they must in their own hearts have felt the equity of the

527
00:34:50,941 --> 00:34:57,520
intention, and must, besides, have been innately conscious that in my place they

528
00:34:57,520 --> 00:34:59,919
would have done precisely what I wished to do.

529
00:35:00,539 --> 00:35:05,779
They yielded at length so far as to consent to put the affair to arbitration.

530
00:35:06,639 --> 00:35:13,960
The judges chosen were Mr. Oliver and an able lawyer, both coincided in my opinion.

531
00:35:14,539 --> 00:35:15,860
I carried my point.

532
00:35:16,479 --> 00:35:22,520
The instruments of transfer were drawn out, Syngin, Diana, Mary and I,

533
00:35:23,179 --> 00:35:25,559
each became possessed of a competency.
